The full string then has $M\sim n m_{\mathrm{link}}
\sim\frac{n}{\ell_s}
\sim\frac{L}{\ell_s^2},
\qquad
L\sim M\ell_s^2.$ Substitution into Equation [eq:l06-string-entropy-length] yields $S_{\mathrm{st}}\sim M\ell_s.$ The lattice walk ignores world-sheet constraints and numerical coefficients, but the exponential growth of the highly excited string spectrum gives this same leading scaling. (Editorial clarification: The random-walk construction is a mnemonic for the high-level density of string states, not a literal discretization of a fundamental string.)

